00:42:25.870 --> 00:42:28.920
But the tweet was already added and I didn't
do it.

00:42:28.920 --> 00:42:31.720
So sorry B-Sides, but I'm doing the shout
out now.

00:42:31.720 --> 00:42:35.310
I will do it next time as well.

00:42:35.310 --> 00:42:36.310
This is far better.

00:42:36.310 --> 00:42:37.820
There will be people watching.

00:42:37.820 --> 00:42:39.240
Yeah, by the way.

00:42:39.240 --> 00:42:41.370
Really good talk by the way.

00:42:41.370 --> 00:42:42.370
So yeah.

00:42:42.370 --> 00:42:45.119
And there will be for this year, it will be
actually, it will be Shops.

00:42:45.119 --> 00:42:47.970
I think you just had an interview with him.

00:42:47.970 --> 00:42:53.090
So Shops will be the keynote speaker and I
think he's a very good researcher.

00:42:53.090 --> 00:42:56.839
It's going to be a really great talk for sure.

00:42:56.839 --> 00:42:57.839
Oh yeah.

00:42:57.839 --> 00:42:58.839
I can't wait.

00:42:58.839 --> 00:42:59.930
I can't wait.

00:42:59.930 --> 00:43:03.660
I saw the recent research about the CCTLDs.

00:43:03.660 --> 00:43:07.020
Yeah, that was insane.

00:43:07.020 --> 00:43:09.540
I loved it.

00:43:09.540 --> 00:43:10.540
Yeah.

00:43:10.540 --> 00:43:14.940
So I know for a fact that you don't stay in
one place for the whole year.

00:43:14.940 --> 00:43:16.240
You travel a lot.

00:43:16.240 --> 00:43:19.270
So tell me what's your current lifestyle?

00:43:19.270 --> 00:43:29.220
So yeah, I mean, I've been doing what we call
digital nomading since 2018.

00:43:29.220 --> 00:43:37.100
So basically, so how it works is that I travel
and at the same time try to work.

00:43:37.100 --> 00:43:38.760
So I've been doing it since 2018.

00:43:38.760 --> 00:43:42.130
I've just been traveling to places.

00:43:42.130 --> 00:43:46.540
So that's been my lifestyle, I mean, for almost
five years.

00:43:46.540 --> 00:43:53.190
But now I'm actually slowing it down a lot
more than I used to before when I was changing

00:43:53.190 --> 00:43:56.960
places more often and it was kind of exhausting.

00:43:56.960 --> 00:43:59.920
And I was not very productive back then.

00:43:59.920 --> 00:44:05.180
But now I'm taking it slow, like with my traveling
and hopefully spend a couple of months in

00:44:05.180 --> 00:44:07.000
each place I go to.

00:44:07.000 --> 00:44:11.470
So that's been my kind of lifestyle for a
few years now.

00:44:11.470 --> 00:44:16.579
What are your favorite places?

00:44:16.579 --> 00:44:21.710
I think I definitely have to go with Southeast
Asia in general.

00:44:21.710 --> 00:44:23.980
I just love it going there.

00:44:23.980 --> 00:44:26.790
And I would say Thailand is one of my favorites.

00:44:26.790 --> 00:44:32.200
Indonesia, I had a really good experience
there as well.

00:44:32.200 --> 00:44:33.960
Vietnam too.

00:44:33.960 --> 00:44:38.329
So these three countries, I really love them.

00:44:38.329 --> 00:44:40.630
So I would say Southeast Asia in general.

00:44:40.630 --> 00:44:46.360
It's just like I feel at home there for some
reason.

00:44:46.360 --> 00:44:51.330
And I love the people there, the culture,
the food.

00:44:51.330 --> 00:44:55.860
It's just overall experience is amazing in
Southeast Asia.

00:44:55.860 --> 00:44:59.930
So those are some of my favorite places for
sure.

00:44:59.930 --> 00:45:02.079
Yeah, I was supposed to go there.

00:45:02.079 --> 00:45:07.140
I wanted to escape winter this time in Poland.

00:45:07.140 --> 00:45:09.100
And my plan was to go to Thailand.

00:45:09.100 --> 00:45:13.630
But I just chickened out before because I
know it's far away, I go alone, blah, blah,

00:45:13.630 --> 00:45:14.630
blah.

00:45:14.630 --> 00:45:17.520
And I saw you on Instagram being in Tenerife.

00:45:17.520 --> 00:45:19.560
And I actually went there because it's closer
to me.

00:45:19.560 --> 00:45:20.560
It's still Europe.

00:45:20.560 --> 00:45:22.450
I speak a bit of Spanish and I absolutely
loved it.

00:45:22.450 --> 00:45:26.460
I will definitely continue in years to come.

00:45:26.460 --> 00:45:31.680
That was I think you did the right choice.

00:45:31.680 --> 00:45:34.510
Tenerife, I've been there as well, was really
good.

00:45:34.510 --> 00:45:35.800
I loved it myself.

00:45:35.800 --> 00:45:37.790
It's just the weather is amazing.

00:45:37.790 --> 00:45:43.441
And it has a huge expat community with so
many digital nomads, like people that you

00:45:43.441 --> 00:45:49.240
can actually meet with so many space, work
spaces where you can work from.

00:45:49.240 --> 00:45:50.740
And just amazing.

00:45:50.740 --> 00:45:54.240
I think you had fun there, right?

00:45:54.240 --> 00:45:55.819
I had lots of fun.

00:45:55.819 --> 00:45:57.030
And the community was the best.

00:45:57.030 --> 00:46:01.130
As I said, I went there alone and I was afraid,
oh, no, maybe I will spend two and a half

00:46:01.130 --> 00:46:04.430
months just sitting in front of my computer
and alone.

00:46:04.430 --> 00:46:11.200
And in reality, I don't think I had so many
friends I would be in touch so often.

00:46:11.200 --> 00:46:12.520
It was completely the opposite.

00:46:12.520 --> 00:46:13.849
And that's what I'm telling people.

00:46:13.849 --> 00:46:20.069
You just get out of your comfort zone and
just like face your fears and go check what's

00:46:20.069 --> 00:46:21.210
out there in the world.

00:46:21.210 --> 00:46:22.599
Just just go in.

00:46:22.599 --> 00:46:24.260
You never know what you're going to experience.

00:46:24.260 --> 00:46:29.470
So you went, you were afraid in the beginning,
but just then you went and you had an extraordinary

00:46:29.470 --> 00:46:30.470
experience with this.

00:46:30.470 --> 00:46:38.920
Yeah, and also you can come back to what we've
talked about previously about the like costs

00:46:38.920 --> 00:46:39.920
of living and things like that.

00:46:39.920 --> 00:46:46.010
You can also go to a country that's not necessarily
worse quality, but it's just cheaper than

00:46:46.010 --> 00:46:51.670
the country you are currently at, depending
on where are you from.

00:46:51.670 --> 00:46:57.680
If I'm if I'm not not mistaken, I think I'm
not the Thailand or Indonesia is just cheaper

00:46:57.680 --> 00:46:59.780
than Europe mostly, right?

00:46:59.780 --> 00:47:02.089
100% actually, it's not as easy.

00:47:02.089 --> 00:47:03.590
It's cheaper than Europe.

00:47:03.590 --> 00:47:05.150
That's that's 100% correct.

00:47:05.150 --> 00:47:11.119
And the thing is that in those places, for
example, you can actually feel the value of

00:47:11.119 --> 00:47:12.490
the dollar that you spend.

00:47:12.490 --> 00:47:20.490
For example, in Bali, if I spend if I spend
600, six bucks, for example, for breakfast,

00:47:20.490 --> 00:47:23.650
I would get the best quality breakfast there.

00:47:23.650 --> 00:47:29.750
So the value, the dollar that you're spending,
there is so much value in it compared to when

00:47:29.750 --> 00:47:36.079
you stay in places that are so expensive in
Europe, you pay loads of money with not much

00:47:36.079 --> 00:47:38.079
value at all.

00:47:38.079 --> 00:47:42.960
And then, like, for example, in those places
in Bali, for example, it's just amazing.

00:47:42.960 --> 00:47:44.150
You pay, you pay.

00:47:44.150 --> 00:47:46.240
I mean, it's getting expensive now.

00:47:46.240 --> 00:47:51.599
It's like this is something that I've started
noticing after the COVID, everyone started

00:47:51.599 --> 00:47:52.630
working remotely.

00:47:52.630 --> 00:47:54.960
So these places are getting crowded now.

00:47:54.960 --> 00:47:58.910
So it's actually getting expensive now, but
not as expensive as in Europe.

00:47:58.910 --> 00:48:03.970
And still, you get a good value out of your
money that you spend there.

00:48:03.970 --> 00:48:06.230
Everything is beautiful there, beautiful beaches.

00:48:06.230 --> 00:48:10.040
You've got co-working spaces everywhere in
Bali, for example.

00:48:10.040 --> 00:48:12.460
You've got a huge expat community.

00:48:12.460 --> 00:48:15.579
If you're feeling bored, you want to go out
and meet people.

00:48:15.579 --> 00:48:22.540
So everything you want is actually there at
a reasonable cost, at a cheaper cost if we

00:48:22.540 --> 00:48:25.710
compare it to Europe, for sure.

00:48:25.710 --> 00:48:27.630
Yeah, that's really awesome.

00:48:27.630 --> 00:48:30.410
But one thing I struggled with was productivity.

00:48:30.410 --> 00:48:37.080
And tell me what are the first things you
do to organize your workspace after arriving

00:48:37.080 --> 00:48:38.790
in a new location?

00:48:38.790 --> 00:48:41.810
Yeah, the productivity is the most important
one.

00:48:41.810 --> 00:48:46.359
Actually, when I first started doing that,
like doing digital nomading, I was not as

00:48:46.359 --> 00:48:48.330
productive as I wanted.

00:48:48.330 --> 00:48:52.069
Because like every time I travel to a new
country, I was like, hey, I need to explore

00:48:52.069 --> 00:48:53.069
it.

00:48:53.069 --> 00:48:57.800
And then explore it, you go check out all
these places, spend a lot of time doing tourist

00:48:57.800 --> 00:48:58.800
stuff.

00:48:58.800 --> 00:49:02.099
And then at night, you go night clubbing,
and then you're not doing anything at the

00:49:02.099 --> 00:49:04.050
end, you're just being a tourist.

00:49:04.050 --> 00:49:05.420
And it took me a while.

00:49:05.420 --> 00:49:10.859
Yeah, it took me a while to go from that tourist
phase to actually go with the mindset that,

00:49:10.859 --> 00:49:12.540
hey, I'm here to work.

00:49:12.540 --> 00:49:13.569
Mainly, that's my priority.

00:49:13.569 --> 00:49:15.260
I set up my mindset.

00:49:15.260 --> 00:49:16.260
I'm here to work.

00:49:16.260 --> 00:49:21.110
And then everything on the side is just like,
it's secondary.

00:49:21.110 --> 00:49:25.230
So I go with the mindset that I need to work
and I need to work out.

00:49:25.230 --> 00:49:27.030
These two are very important.

00:49:27.030 --> 00:49:33.220
And then if I've got spare time, then I can
go chill, visit places, meet people.

00:49:33.220 --> 00:49:39.970
And when I go to a place, I mean, like when
I'm doing this lifestyle, if I want to be

00:49:39.970 --> 00:49:44.059
productive, I would straight go to an Airbnb,
for example.

00:49:44.059 --> 00:49:50.940
I get my own privacy and I make sure there
is a good Wi-Fi there, like a fiber optic

00:49:50.940 --> 00:49:54.930
Wi-Fi that will not be interrupting.

00:49:54.930 --> 00:49:59.000
And I make sure there is a desk where I can
work myself.

00:49:59.000 --> 00:50:04.319
And or just if I don't have like a decent
Airbnb, I make sure to look up if there are

00:50:04.319 --> 00:50:09.960
co-working spaces in the city that I'm going
to beforehand so that I can just go work straight

00:50:09.960 --> 00:50:10.960
there.

00:50:10.960 --> 00:50:15.420
If I'm having meetings with my clients, you
need to apply a place that is quiet and where

00:50:15.420 --> 00:50:16.650
you can get things done.

00:50:16.650 --> 00:50:21.541
So you need to do research beforehand or just
look for if there are some cafes where you

00:50:21.541 --> 00:50:26.950
can work from and they tolerate people with
laptops because not all cafes can just let

00:50:26.950 --> 00:50:28.819
you work there all day.

00:50:28.819 --> 00:50:33.840
So you need to do some research before you
go to that place and just make sure to stick

00:50:33.840 --> 00:50:36.380
to the regular schedule.

00:50:36.380 --> 00:50:40.980
Like you make sure you wake up in the morning,
grab your breakfast and go straight to work.

00:50:40.980 --> 00:50:46.020
It would be preferable if you actually go
to a working space because you put yourself

00:50:46.020 --> 00:50:49.310
in the work mindset instead of you just stay
at home.

00:50:49.310 --> 00:50:51.329
It can be confusing a bit.

00:50:51.329 --> 00:50:55.680
So if you've got that option, you find a place
that is affordable, definitely my recommendation

00:50:55.680 --> 00:50:59.809
is to go work from a workspace because you're
going to see other people's workings.

00:50:59.809 --> 00:51:03.790
You're going to force yourself to actually
to work as well and you're just going to stick

00:51:03.790 --> 00:51:04.790
to the schedule.

00:51:04.790 --> 00:51:09.500
Maybe once you hit 5 p.m. then you give yourself
a break and you can go grab some drinks with

00:51:09.500 --> 00:51:12.520
people or just chill at home.

00:51:12.520 --> 00:51:16.619
So just try to stick to that schedule and
don't get distracted.

00:51:16.619 --> 00:51:20.859
Especially if you have someone to travel with
that is also like have the same goal, that

00:51:20.859 --> 00:51:22.950
would be a lot better.

00:51:22.950 --> 00:51:24.710
So you can just motivate yourselves.

00:51:24.710 --> 00:51:26.340
Yeah, yeah.

00:51:26.340 --> 00:51:31.930
I actually really liked working from a coworking
space or a co-living space as well.

00:51:31.930 --> 00:51:35.530
It was definitely a good experience.

00:51:35.530 --> 00:51:36.530
100%.

00:51:36.530 --> 00:51:38.040
And I also felt...

00:51:38.040 --> 00:51:41.329
Yeah, yeah, go ahead, sorry.

00:51:41.329 --> 00:51:47.960
I was just going to say it's like a close
family, especially if you're doing the co-living

00:51:47.960 --> 00:51:48.960
thing.

00:51:48.960 --> 00:51:53.300
It's just like living with the same people
for a couple of weeks and you just start bonding

00:51:53.300 --> 00:51:56.230
and just like feeling closer together.

00:51:56.230 --> 00:51:57.230
It's amazing.

00:51:57.230 --> 00:51:58.970
Go ahead, sorry for interrupting.

00:51:58.970 --> 00:52:04.359
Yeah, I had no idea what co-living is before
and I really, really liked it.

00:52:04.359 --> 00:52:10.440
I wanted to ask you if, because I felt like
for this kind of lifestyle, I would rather

00:52:10.440 --> 00:52:16.190
do pen tests and I would have some particular
specific project that I have to finish until

00:52:16.190 --> 00:52:24.640
a specific day rather than having a bug bounty,
which is very hard to organize into a deadline

00:52:24.640 --> 00:52:25.640
or something.

00:52:25.640 --> 00:52:27.570
I completely agree with you.

00:52:27.570 --> 00:52:33.600
Actually when I started in 2018, I was already
working with HackerOne on the side.

00:52:33.600 --> 00:52:40.400
For me that was helpful because I could just
do my work with HackerOne and do not have

00:52:40.400 --> 00:52:43.240
to care that much for finding bugs.

00:52:43.240 --> 00:52:47.040
But I was also doing bug bounties on the side
as well, so that helped a bit.

00:52:47.040 --> 00:52:50.130
And I completely agree that if you're going
to do this lifestyle, it's much better to

00:52:50.130 --> 00:52:54.589
have something that you can rely on because
when you're traveling, you have so many expenses

00:52:54.589 --> 00:52:59.670
that are just piling up and there are some
unexpected expenses sometimes, just like a

00:52:59.670 --> 00:53:05.800
flight getting canceled, a hotel, just raising
prices in hotels.

00:53:05.800 --> 00:53:10.960
There are so many unexpected expenses, so
it's much better for your mental health to

00:53:10.960 --> 00:53:16.160
just have something that you can rely on for
some revenue and then you can always do bug

00:53:16.160 --> 00:53:17.160
bounties.

00:53:17.160 --> 00:53:24.450
But I mean, if you've got the skill set, you
know yourself, you're good, you could go without

00:53:24.450 --> 00:53:28.589
finding anything for a month and then you're
going to find that one good bug that will

00:53:28.589 --> 00:53:29.589
pay for your expenses.

00:53:29.589 --> 00:53:31.780
I think that's fine as well.

00:53:31.780 --> 00:53:35.790
So it depends on the person, but I think it
would be preferable if you have something

00:53:35.790 --> 00:53:40.820
you can rely on for sure, 100%.

00:53:40.820 --> 00:53:42.000
What's your hardware setup?

00:53:42.000 --> 00:53:46.869
And I'm mostly interested in if you use an
external screen.

00:53:46.869 --> 00:53:52.950
No, this is something that people actually
think funny about me because I always use

00:53:52.950 --> 00:53:55.530
my MacBook laptop.

00:53:55.530 --> 00:53:57.700
I don't use any external monitors.

00:53:57.700 --> 00:54:05.369
I just actually recently, last year, I bought
my very first monitor because I'm traveling.

00:54:05.369 --> 00:54:09.670
I left it at home, so I barely use it, only
when I go back to visit.

00:54:09.670 --> 00:54:18.349
But for all these years, I just use my small
MacBook laptop, no crazy external monitors

00:54:18.349 --> 00:54:19.349
or anything.

00:54:19.349 --> 00:54:20.349
It works for me.

00:54:20.349 --> 00:54:26.579
I mean, I do feel like I would be a bit more
protective if I use an external screen sometimes,

00:54:26.579 --> 00:54:34.020
but it also does not bother me that much and
it's not going to make that huge difference.

00:54:34.020 --> 00:54:41.270
But I think it's definitely more convenient
when you have a screen on the side that you

00:54:41.270 --> 00:54:42.270
can use.

00:54:42.270 --> 00:54:44.450
But yeah, for all these years, I've only used
my small laptop.

00:54:44.450 --> 00:54:48.720
At one point, I had a 13-inch MacBook.

00:54:48.720 --> 00:54:50.420
Now I have a 14-inch.

00:54:50.420 --> 00:54:53.640
What are your tips for people working with
a single monitor?

00:54:53.640 --> 00:54:59.329
I'm not sure I really have any tips.

00:54:59.329 --> 00:55:01.349
It just depends how many screens you open.

00:55:01.349 --> 00:55:03.730
I only open the one browser.

00:55:03.730 --> 00:55:10.990
I mean, I open Chrome and then I open the
Burp suite, so I don't really find it hard

00:55:10.990 --> 00:55:13.859
to browse between the two.

00:55:13.859 --> 00:55:16.890
So it's not really a huge concern.

00:55:16.890 --> 00:55:18.869
But it depends.

00:55:18.869 --> 00:55:23.530
But I would assume for someone like you, you
might need some...

00:55:23.530 --> 00:55:27.450
For someone like you with the editing, with
other things that you're doing, you probably

00:55:27.450 --> 00:55:31.160
would need an external screen, right?

00:55:31.160 --> 00:55:33.380
Yeah, yeah.

00:55:33.380 --> 00:55:36.369
I also work quite a lot with...

00:55:36.369 --> 00:55:41.690
Even in my home right now, I just have an
ultrawide monitor plus the MacBook normal

00:55:41.690 --> 00:55:45.510
monitor and I kind of work only on the ultrawide.

00:55:45.510 --> 00:55:50.910
And I've noticed that I just use the desktops
a lot and I switch between them.

00:55:50.910 --> 00:55:56.210
And what I think is unless you are actually
doing something in one window and looking

00:55:56.210 --> 00:56:02.500
at the result in another window, I think you
don't need external monitors to switch.

00:56:02.500 --> 00:56:07.609
If you have like Burp open and the browser
open and you don't need to see at this literally

00:56:07.609 --> 00:56:11.240
at the same time both, I think you're just
perfectly fine.

00:56:11.240 --> 00:56:16.360
Because switching desktop is pretty much the
same time as switching your eyes.

00:56:16.360 --> 00:56:18.390
And I get easily adjusted to this.

00:56:18.390 --> 00:56:20.720
But for editing, yes, you need...

00:56:20.720 --> 00:56:24.030
I don't think you need a lot of screens.

00:56:24.030 --> 00:56:28.540
You just need a big screen and my 14 inch
is not enough.

00:56:28.540 --> 00:56:30.140
Yeah, 100%.

00:56:30.140 --> 00:56:32.730
I think if you can just adapt, I think it's
possible.

00:56:32.730 --> 00:56:34.590
It's nothing crazy.

00:56:34.590 --> 00:56:40.200
Also, I just, for example, open two screens
on my laptop and I just swipe between the

00:56:40.200 --> 00:56:46.730
two like I put my Burp suite on the right
window and my Chrome browser on the left,

00:56:46.730 --> 00:56:49.130
I actually just swipe between the two.

00:56:49.130 --> 00:56:51.390
That makes it easier for me.

00:56:51.390 --> 00:56:55.660
Also, if you're traveling, there are some
co-working spaces where you can rent a screen,

00:56:55.660 --> 00:56:56.660
for example.

00:56:56.660 --> 00:57:00.470
They do rent screens, monitors, so you can
do that as well.

00:57:00.470 --> 00:57:07.220
Otherwise, I think I know some people that
use a huge iPad, use their laptop and then

00:57:07.220 --> 00:57:10.119
iPad that works for them.

00:57:10.119 --> 00:57:12.020
Yeah.

00:57:12.020 --> 00:57:19.540
I did rent some screens and I saw, I think
I just saw an ad of like foldable triple external

00:57:19.540 --> 00:57:21.789
screens that are like the size of a MacBook.

00:57:21.789 --> 00:57:29.140
But I haven't tested it, but I don't think
I actually need this.

00:57:29.140 --> 00:57:34.490
Another thing that I saw is I actually wanted
to see what are you up to on your Instagram,

00:57:34.490 --> 00:57:36.410
but I think you deleted one.

00:57:36.410 --> 00:57:39.099
What's your relationship with social media?

00:57:39.099 --> 00:57:41.160
Okay, I actually disabled it.

00:57:41.160 --> 00:57:47.960
I disabled it because I wanted to focus a
bit on work and not have too many distractions.

00:57:47.960 --> 00:57:54.260
So my relationship with social media, I think
it's a healthy one, but I had to work to get

00:57:54.260 --> 00:57:58.599
there actually because there were times where
I was very addicted to social media.

00:57:58.599 --> 00:58:03.500
For example, like Facebook, I would post a
lot there.

00:58:03.500 --> 00:58:05.700
And then I got rid of Facebook in 2020.

00:58:05.700 --> 00:58:07.400
I disabled it indefinitely.

00:58:07.400 --> 00:58:10.150
I never get there anymore.

00:58:10.150 --> 00:58:13.170
Then I kept my Instagram and Twitter.

00:58:13.170 --> 00:58:14.860
I use it professionally.

00:58:14.860 --> 00:58:19.289
So Twitter has been very helpful, just building
the community there and interacting with like

00:58:19.289 --> 00:58:20.480
minded people.

00:58:20.480 --> 00:58:27.850
So I only exclusively use it to that and sometimes
post some updates and just get some info there.

00:58:27.850 --> 00:58:29.950
So I use Twitter professionally.

00:58:29.950 --> 00:58:36.070
I use Instagram to post my travel adventures
or travel pictures.

00:58:36.070 --> 00:58:42.660
I love Instagram because I use it as a, it's
just like a book where I post all my past

00:58:42.660 --> 00:58:47.099
travels and just like for a memory thing.

00:58:47.099 --> 00:58:52.400
Some people think that I'm trying to do the
influencing thing, but I couldn't care about

00:58:52.400 --> 00:58:53.400
that.

00:58:53.400 --> 00:58:58.119
I love Instagram to post my stories there
and every time, save them to the highlight

00:58:58.119 --> 00:59:04.660
and I go back and just can check everything
I've done in a trip, for example.

00:59:04.660 --> 00:59:07.130
So yeah, I use Instagram more moderately.

00:59:07.130 --> 00:59:11.220
I don't scroll up and down and watch reels
indefinitely.

00:59:11.220 --> 00:59:14.710
I just post a story and that's it.

00:59:14.710 --> 00:59:15.710
Yeah.

00:59:15.710 --> 00:59:21.160
And also I do some periods where I just stop
using social media once and for all, like

00:59:21.160 --> 00:59:22.680
for a month or for two months.

00:59:22.680 --> 00:59:26.880
For example, this year I think I've done it
a couple of months.

00:59:26.880 --> 00:59:30.829
Last year I stopped using social media for
three months.

00:59:30.829 --> 00:59:40.829
These periods actually just help me detox
from these things as well as just like get

00:59:40.829 --> 00:59:46.620
rid of distractions so I can focus a bit more
on work and be productive in other areas of

00:59:46.620 --> 00:59:47.620
life.

00:59:47.620 --> 00:59:48.620
Yeah.

00:59:48.620 --> 00:59:49.620
Okay.

00:59:49.620 --> 00:59:59.020
You also posted, when you were there, posted
quite a lot of updates from the gym.

00:59:59.020 --> 01:00:05.690
How often do you do sports and what type of
sports?

01:00:05.690 --> 01:00:07.440
I love sports a lot.

01:00:07.440 --> 01:00:09.680
So I do different kinds of sports.

01:00:09.680 --> 01:00:10.900
I do running.

01:00:10.900 --> 01:00:12.789
I run half marathons.

01:00:12.789 --> 01:00:16.680
I do a lot of running, actually, like 10Ks,
20K.

01:00:16.680 --> 01:00:23.359
I do weightlifting as well, maybe four to
five.

01:00:23.359 --> 01:00:26.530
I do like five sessions or six sessions a
week.

01:00:26.530 --> 01:00:28.610
I love hiking as well.

01:00:28.610 --> 01:00:33.520
I do trekking, just like hiking mountains
for a couple of days.

01:00:33.520 --> 01:00:35.000
Surf skating as well.

01:00:35.000 --> 01:00:41.110
Currently, I'm actually trying to learn surfing
and that's one of the things that I was doing

01:00:41.110 --> 01:00:43.049
in Tenerife when I was there myself.

01:00:43.049 --> 01:00:48.480
So I love Tenerife because like you have the
mountains, so I would go and run in the mountains

01:00:48.480 --> 01:00:49.480
and hike there.

01:00:49.480 --> 01:00:51.160
And then we have the ocean as well.

01:00:51.160 --> 01:00:52.559
You can just go for surfing.

01:00:52.559 --> 01:00:53.960
I love surfing there.

01:00:53.960 --> 01:00:56.619
Amazing and consistent waves.

01:00:56.619 --> 01:00:59.490
So I'm trying to learn surfing as well.

01:00:59.490 --> 01:01:02.350
And I do other stuff on the side.

01:01:02.350 --> 01:01:06.490
So I love sports and I just feel like it helps
me be a better person.

01:01:06.490 --> 01:01:14.640
So I'm doing it regularly and I feel it has
huge, amazing outcomes on my life.

01:01:14.640 --> 01:01:18.000
It just changed my life for the best.

01:01:18.000 --> 01:01:23.450
Just like being in good shape, thinking clearly,
having the mental clarity.

01:01:23.450 --> 01:01:29.569
Just like a couple of weeks ago, I was just
feeling a bit of a brain fog and then I just

01:01:29.569 --> 01:01:35.940
like doubled down on my exercising, started
doing some intermittent fasting and it actually

01:01:35.940 --> 01:01:36.940
helped a lot.

01:01:36.940 --> 01:01:39.349
I feel a lot better now, can think very clearly.

01:01:39.349 --> 01:01:45.530
So I think doing sports have actually changed
my life for the best and I definitely encourage

01:01:45.530 --> 01:01:47.980
everyone else to do some sort of activity.

01:01:47.980 --> 01:01:55.529
But whatever it is, as long as you're just
keeping yourself active, burning those calories

01:01:55.529 --> 01:02:03.990
and making your heart work and getting strong.

01:02:03.990 --> 01:02:08.630
Could you recommend some specific activities
for people that are listening to us?

01:02:08.630 --> 01:02:13.039
They maybe spent whole days in front of the
computer and they don't really move much and

01:02:13.039 --> 01:02:16.099
they would like to do something with their
life, maybe lose some weight.

01:02:16.099 --> 01:02:18.809
What are some fun things they can do?

01:02:18.809 --> 01:02:24.490
Yes, I think there are so many activities
that you can do that would actually fit your

01:02:24.490 --> 01:02:26.529
schedule or fit your budget.

01:02:26.529 --> 01:02:31.180
For example, if you don't feel like going
to the gym or you feel like if you go there,

01:02:31.180 --> 01:02:35.750
you'd be confused, the first thing you can
just go out there, put on your shoes and just

01:02:35.750 --> 01:02:40.230
go run, maybe run three kilometers in the
beginning.

01:02:40.230 --> 01:02:45.660
Don't go hard on yourself, just run at a very
slow pace where you can maintain a conversation

01:02:45.660 --> 01:02:47.119
with someone else.

01:02:47.119 --> 01:02:53.079
And just run for three kilometers, that's
already something very good that you did and

01:02:53.079 --> 01:02:57.260
then you can progressively increase the mileage
over time.

01:02:57.260 --> 01:03:02.160
So running is a very simple activity that
you can do at your own pace, you don't have

01:03:02.160 --> 01:03:12.210
to go faster to the extent that you hate it,
just make sure you're trying to learn and

01:03:12.210 --> 01:03:13.609
enjoy at the same time.

01:03:13.609 --> 01:03:19.099
So I would suggest just running and then if
you can afford the gym, it's not as expensive

01:03:19.099 --> 01:03:23.119
as you might think, you just get a gym subscription.

01:03:23.119 --> 01:03:30.589
There are loads of YouTube videos that you
can watch on how you can perform some different

01:03:30.589 --> 01:03:32.089
exercises in the gym.

01:03:32.089 --> 01:03:37.099
You don't need to use free weights, for example,
there are so many machines that are very easy

01:03:37.099 --> 01:03:44.530
to use in the gym, you don't need any knowledge
or just watch some YouTube videos.

01:03:44.530 --> 01:03:50.540
There are so many, I would say, workouts on
YouTube, you could just do like a 20 minutes

01:03:50.540 --> 01:03:57.230
workout and after that workout, you will feel
so much better, you will think very clearly

01:03:57.230 --> 01:04:00.440
and that will help you as a backbone hunter.

01:04:00.440 --> 01:04:05.441
Like being in a good shape will definitely
help a lot more than you think because I think

01:04:05.441 --> 01:04:07.390
a lot of people are neglecting their health.

01:04:07.390 --> 01:04:12.420
Because I noticed myself back in 2017, 2018,
I was struggling a lot.

01:04:12.420 --> 01:04:19.670
I didn't care that much about my own health,
I was not regularly exercising and I can always

01:04:19.670 --> 01:04:26.410
like compare it to now where I maintain a
very regular exercising schedule, I eat a

01:04:26.410 --> 01:04:31.630
clean diet, I can compare it to that period
and there is so much difference.

01:04:31.630 --> 01:04:41.440
I just feel like my life has upgraded immensely
just by changing my lifestyle and exercising

01:04:41.440 --> 01:04:44.599
and making sure I eat a clean diet.

01:04:44.599 --> 01:04:50.450
So I think 100% will definitely help you be
a better version of yourself either as a bug

01:04:50.450 --> 01:04:57.070
hunter or just a good person trying to live
their lives and do things in life.

01:04:57.070 --> 01:05:03.490
Yeah, that's very nicely said and I also encourage
everyone definitely to do sports.

01:05:03.490 --> 01:05:05.930
I personally also love doing sports.

01:05:05.930 --> 01:05:09.230
I'm just happy doing them, I feel good in
my body.

01:05:09.230 --> 01:05:14.520
I have lots of fun with friends doing different
types of activities.

01:05:14.520 --> 01:05:19.640
So I definitely encourage everyone and I guarantee
that you will take the time off the schedule

01:05:19.640 --> 01:05:25.930
but you will actually be more productive and
you will probably still do more in the same

01:05:25.930 --> 01:05:26.930
amount of time.

01:05:26.930 --> 01:05:29.220
You will have much more fun as well.

01:05:29.220 --> 01:05:30.960
100% exactly.

